vides data to drive campaign performance; Custom Contextual solution, which allows advertisers to match ads to relevant content to maximize user engagement and drive campaign performance; and Scibids AI, an AI-powered digital campaign optimization solution. It also provides Rockerbox, enables advertisers to unify cross-channel conversion and spend data and apply multi-touch attribution, marketing mix modeling, and incrementality testing to measure and optimize the impact of advertising; DV Authentic AdVantage, an AI-powered performance optimization solution for advertisers to improve campaign outcomes across proprietary video platforms; DV Publisher Suite, a unified solution for digital publishers to manage revenue and increase inventory yield, identifying lost or unfilled sales, and aggregate data across inventory sources; and DV Pinnacle which provides detailed insights into customers' media performance on both direct and programmatic media buying platforms and across all key digital media channels, formats, and devices. Its solutions are integrated across digital advertising ecosystem, including programmatic platforms, social media channels, and digital publishers. The company serves consumer packaged goods, financial services, telecommunications, technology, automotive, and healthcare industry verticals. The company was founded in 2008 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark S. Zagorski | CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $608K ranks in the below the sector median among Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 22%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $140K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $85K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["DoubleVerify Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap communication services business with a $2.1B market cap on $748M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $173M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 23 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.17\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 46\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 6.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 14% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 33% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.33322149312037874},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (38% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Communication Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Communication Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Is Drawing Fresh Attention To DoubleVerify Holdings (DV)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/media/nyse-dv/doubleverify-holdings/news/what-is-drawing-fresh-attention-to-doubleverify-holdings-dv","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793820346.208,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.94,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Should DoubleVerify Holdings (DV) Investors Care About Its Merger And New AI Tools?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/media-advertising/articles/doubleverify-holdings-dv-investors-care-110926686.html","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793531366.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"DoubleVerify (DV) Q3 Earnings Keep Profit Growth In Focus","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/media/nyse-dv/doubleverify-holdings/news/doubleverify-dv-q3-earnings-keep-profit-growth-in-focus","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793496100.069,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.95,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title